!Sample_title = ECCITE-seq cDNA Rep2_Lane1: A549-ACE2
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM4831696
!Sample_status = Public on Oct 24 2020
!Sample_submission_date = Oct 19 2020
!Sample_last_update_date = Oct 25 2020
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = ECCITE-seq cDNA: A549-ACE2
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: A549
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: human alveolar basal epithelial carcinoma cell line
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype/variation: trangenic ACE2 overexpression
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Lentivirus was produced via transfection of the minipool with appropriate packaging plasmids (psPAX2: Addgene 12260; pMD2.G: Addgene 12259) using polyethylenimine (PEI) reagent in HEK293FT. The target A549ACE2 cells were transduced in presence of polybrene (10 μg/mL, Santa Cruz) (ECCITE-Seq replicate 1) or without (ECCITE-seq replicate 2) at very low MOI to ensure entry of a single virus per cell. The survival was below 5% after 2 days of selection with 2 μg/mL puromycin (Thermo) for both ECCITE-seq experiments. On day 10 post-transduction, the cells were collected and processed for ECCITE-seq.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Human alveolar basal epithelial carcinoma cells (A549, ATCC CCL-185) were maintained at 37C and 5% CO2 in D10 media, which consists of DMEM (Caisson Labs) with 10% Serum Plus II Medium Supplement (Sigma-Aldrich)
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = polyA RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = ECCITE-seq (10x genomics 5prime V1): We divided the ECCITE-seq pool into several sub-pools and performed cell-hashing. Cell hashing was performed as described in a previously published protocol (Mimitou et al., 2019). For the ECCITE-seq experiment, we ran four lanes of a 10x Genomics 5’ kit (Chromium Single Cell Immune Profiling Solution v1.0, #1000014, #1000020, #1000151) targeting recovery of 12,000 cells per lane (superloading) in experiment 1 and 20,000 cells in experiment 2. Gene expression (mRNA), hashtags (Hashtag-derived oligos, HTOs) and guide RNA (Guide-derived oligos, GDOs) libraries were constructed by following 10x Genomics and ECCITE-seq protocols.
!Sample_description = cDNA_Rep2_Lane1
!Sample_data_processing = library strategy: ECCITE-seq (Expanded CRISPR-compatible Cellular Indexing of Transcriptomes and Epitopes by sequencing)
!Sample_data_processing = ECCITE-seq RNA reads were mapped to the human genome (hg38, ensembl v97). Transcripts were quanitfied using CellRanger v3.0.1
!Sample_data_processing = HTO and GDO counts were quantified using CITE-seq-count v1.4.2. (https://github.com/Hoohm/CITE-seq-Count)
!Sample_data_processing = Cells were demultiplexed based on their HTO counts into their experimental conditions after normalization (centered log ratio transformation, margin = 2) using the HTOdemux or MULTISeqDemux function in Seurat.
!Sample_data_processing = gRNA identitied were assigned using MULTISeqDemux unless otherwise specified in the methods section of the manuscript.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: hg38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Processed data provided in standard CellRanger output format for cDNA, GDO, and HTO. Each sample has 3 tab separated files separate into features, barcodes and a sparse matrix file.
